  "title": "Ground beef hardshell tacos",
  "description": null,
  "editorial": {
    "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>These are to die for tacos. I've made it so many times and each time, it turns out so great. It goes awesome with <a href=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/recipe/virgin-mojito-2/\">Virgin Mojito</a>.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe {\"id\":21280,\"template\":\"chic-template-english\",\"updated\":1659212681427} -->\n<!--WPRM Recipe 21280-->\n<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe\">\n\t<h2 class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-name\">Ground beef hardshell tacos</h2>\n\t<img class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-image\" src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/01/50327270_333702840809989_1716025333821472768_n.Blog_-150x150.png\"/>\t<p class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-summary\">\n\t\t\t</p>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-equipment\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-ingredients\">\n\t\t<ul><li>1 lb ground beef</li><li>3 Tbsp taco seasoning</li><li>5 Tbsp cold water</li><li>1/2 cup cheese (shredded )</li><li>2 cups lettuce (shredded )</li><li>1/2 cup cilantro</li><li>1/2 cup salsa</li><li>1/2 cup sour cream</li><li>10 taco shells (hard)</li></ul>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-instructions\">\n\t\t<ol><li>Fully cook the ground beef. Drain extra grease. Add water and taco seasoning then cook for 3 more minutes.<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/01/50401035_2009728035802762_8561041981927587840_n.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Dice tomatoes.<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/01/50074670_243980343165870_1221729706777247744_n.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Cut avocado into small cubes.<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/01/49938147_245928209639609_2722087093235875840_n.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Shred lettuce.<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/01/50458345_770127170033750_3464197187888480256_n.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Finely chop cilantro.<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/01/49947198_632187110528893_1163584229070602240_n.Blog_-e1547659240381-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Meanwhile, preheat oven to 375 degrees F. Place empty taco shells on a cooking sheet and bake for 5 minutes.<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/01/50051916_331464617700473_9109905967331409920_n-150x150.jpg\"/><br /></li><li>Assemble each taco with meat mixture, tomatoes, avocado, cilantro and lettuce. Top it with sour cream and salsa. Sprinkle with shredded cheese. Serve immediately. <br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/01/50327270_333702840809989_1716025333821472768_n.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li></ol>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-notes\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta\">\n\t\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta-course\">Main Dish</div>\t</div>\n</div>\n<!--End WPRM Recipe-->\n<!-- /wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe -->",
    "excerpt": null
  },
